{
  "title": "Structural Stability Visualiser",
  "slug": "stability",
  "version": 1,
  "summary": "Explore column buckling (Euler, Johnson, optional tangent modulus), second-order beam-columns (secant-type first-yield root finder with a beam FE eigenvalue cross-check), flat-plate shear buckling with the NACA TN 3781 plasticity factor, and NACA TN 2661 diagonal tension on plane webs with pure Wagner tension as the k = 1 limit.",
  "disclaimer": "Not for certification. Exploration and preliminary sizing only: no design allowables, no knockdown factors, illustrative material presets. Check every result independently.",
  "units": "Stored canonically in N, mm and MPa (N/mm²). The SI/US switch (N·mm·MPa or lbf·in·ksi) changes display and entry only, so exported files stay canonical SI.",
  "source_policy": [
    "NASA: the relation is stated in the cited NASA/NACA report and section.",
    "classical: no NASA source was found; the relation is textbook engineering mechanics and is never presented as NASA-derived.",
    "fit: a closed form fitted to a NASA report figure; the digitised points are in figures below and the fit error is shown on the page.",
    "A chart-based relation outside its figure's range shows 'unavailable: chart data not sourced'. No value is guessed: kss beyond fig. 12(a) (hc/dc above 5) makes the web buckling stress and every later diagonal-tension result unavailable, and fig. 15 beyond d/hU = 1 and fig. 18 beyond ωd = 4 are unavailable.",
    "The one exception is fig. 12(b) beyond t/t = 3, held at its end value because NACA TN 2661 section 7, example 1, p. 57 applies that hold (tU/t = 3.20 and tF/t large give Rh = Rd = 1.62); the hold is tagged with that source and warned. Below the solid part of fig. 12(b) the dashed part drawn in the figure is used, with a warning."
  ],
  "tabs": {
    "column": "Euler and Johnson column curves with the transition slenderness, an optional tangent-modulus curve from the Ramberg-Osgood fit, Pcr and the margin of safety against the entered load.",
    "beamColumn": "Pin-ended second-order beam-column of length KL under eccentric axial load, end moments, uniform lateral load and an initial bow (default L/1000, flagged as an assumption). A bracketed Newton root finder with bisection fallback solves σmax = P/A + Mmax/S = Fcy for the first-yield load. A 24-element beam FE model with geometric stiffness and a hand-written Jacobi eigen routine gives Pcr for the K presets and for end springs.",
    "shear": "Flat isotropic rectangular plates in shear with simply supported or clamped edges, closed-form k_s(a/b), and the NACA TN 3781 plasticity-reduction factor on the Ramberg-Osgood curve.",
    "diagonal": "NACA TN 2661 incomplete diagonal tension on plane webs: effective upright area, web buckling stress with the report's restraint coefficients, diagonal-tension factor k, angle of diagonal tension, upright, flange and web stresses, the peak web stress and the upright column check; pure Wagner diagonal tension (TN 469) is shown as the k = 1 limit."
  },
  "not_in_scope": [
    "Curved webs and panels",
    "Orthotropic or stiffened plates",
    "Forced crippling of uprights",
    "Flange secondary bending",
    "Rivet checks",
    "Allowable web stress (TN 2661 fig. 19)",
    "Certification allowables",
    "Plastic-hinge or interaction-curve beam-column criteria",
    "NASA source-code ports"
  ],
  "reference_notes": [
    "NTRS returned HTTP 403 to automated downloads when these checks were made, so the report scans were read from mirrors of the same NACA documents (everyspec.com and OSTI); citations give the NTRS document IDs.",
    "TN 2661 defines its own edge-restraint coefficients Rh and Rd (section 3.6, eq. 32; R = 1 simply supported, 1.62 clamped; empirical values in fig. 12(b)), so they replace the 0-to-1 fixity blend: Rh and Rd come from the fig. 12(b) fit or are typed in.",
    "TN 2661 takes the plastic web buckling stress from fig. 12(c), drawn only for 24S-T3 and 75S-T6. The page uses the TN 3781 eq. (A5) factor on the entered Ramberg-Osgood curve instead, so example 2's plastic τcr (16.10 ksi in the report) is not reproduced; its later steps are checked at the report's k.",
    "TN 3781 gives two shear plasticity factors: appendix A and fig. 10 use η = (Es/E)(1 − νe²)/(1 − ν²) (eq. A5); table 2 multiplies it by 0.83 + 0.17 Et/Es. A5 is the default; table 2 is an option.",
    "TN 2661 example 2 prints τcr,elastic = 16.55 ksi, but eq. (32) with its printed inputs gives 16.28 ksi (1.7 % lower). It also prints hc/d = 1.50 while hc/dc = 9.875/7 = 1.41; the printed kss = 6.70 matches fig. 12(a) at 1.41.",
    "TN 2661 section 4.2 note 2 (use the buckling stress with the uprights disregarded when it is higher) is not checked: the report gives no kss for the uprights-disregarded (infinitely long) panel, so that stress is unavailable, τcr uses eq. (32) with the uprights, and a warning says note 2 could not be checked.",
    "The closed-form k_s(a/b) are classical approximations (Timoshenko and Gere); TN 3781 gives k_s only as a chart (fig. 22). They reproduce the exact square-plate values 9.34 (simply supported) and about 14.6 against 14.71 (clamped).",
    "The fixed-pinned FE Pcr is 0.24 % above π²EI/(0.7L)² because the exact effective-length factor is 0.699, not 0.7."
  ],
